From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:35:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wifi: mt76: DEBUG: count the register reads of the TX
 path

Add debug counters in struct mt76_dev to price and locate register reads
on the TX path of mt76 devices (in particular mt76x02 on PCIe):

- mt76_dma_tx_cleanup: calls per queue, calls on empty queue, first index
  reads, catch-up re-reads, and entries completed per queue;
- T3 descriptor walk and fallback counters: clean_done_walk,
  clean_done_idx, walk_empty, fallback_progress, desc_reads per queue;
- T3 shadow mode (mode 1) counters: shadow_missing,
  shadow_missing_after_next, shadow_ooo (out-of-order completions),
  shadow_unverifiable (reused slots), shadow_missing_overflow,
  shadow_early, and shadow_max_gap;
- T3 verify mode (mode 3) and index safety counters: walk_behind,
  walk_ahead, walk_max_behind, walk_max_ahead, index_behind,
  index_max_behind, and index_ambiguous;
- mt76x02_poll_tx / mt7603_poll_tx: polls and entries completed in the
  first and second passes;
- mt76x02_mac_poll_tx_status: calls per caller (IRQ, TX NAPI, TX worker,
  mt76x02_tx_complete_skb), valid status reads and empty reads;
- tx_hang index reads and interrupts handled;
- total mmio_rr calls across the device.

Expose the counters via debugfs file 'tx_reads' (writing any value resets
all counters), 'rr_cost' (pricing register reads over bus/PCIe, coherent
DMA descriptor uncached read, and cached RAM read), and 'desc_rd_cost'
(pricing uncached descriptor control word read latency).

Debug instrumentation only, never in the release image.
